<%# Drives the SHIPPED wallet identity source in a real browser.

    THE PAGE CARRIES NO SOURCE LOGIC. It does the two things a HOST does with
    SolanaStudio.walletIdentity and nothing else: it registers the source with a
    session store, and it paints what the source reports, the way a navbar would.
    The wallets are the SPEC's, installed by page.addInitScript before this page's
    scripts run, which is how a real extension injects its provider.

    THE SESSION STORE IS A RECORDER, not studio-engine's store. The engine's
    session.js is not in any released studio-engine yet, so the lab cannot load it
    from the installed gem. The recorder only calls source.start(report) and keeps
    what arrives: it compares nothing, so it cannot decide a mismatch on the gem's
    behalf. Mismatch, resolve and hold semantics are the node suite's stub and a
    run against the real engine store; this page proves the shipped bytes RUN.

    `?provider=lab` makes the source watch window.labWallet instead of Phantom's
    injected global, so one page serves both the default resolver and a host's. %>
<main data-test="wallet-identity-lab">
  <p data-test="identity-loaded"><%= "" %></p>
  <p data-test="wallet-status">not started</p>
  <p data-test="wallet-provider"><%= "" %></p>
</main>

<script>
  (function () {
    var S = window.SolanaStudio || {};
    document.querySelector('[data-test="identity-loaded"]').textContent =
      S.walletIdentity ? 'loaded' : 'MISSING: walletIdentity';
    if (!S.walletIdentity) return;

    window.labReports = [];
    var recorder = {
      registerIdentitySource: function (source) {
        var stop = source.start(function (value) {
          window.labReports.push(value === undefined ? 'undefined' : value);
        });
        return { name: source.name, unregister: function () { if (typeof stop === 'function') stop(); } };
      }
    };

    var options = { session: recorder };
    if (new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('provider') === 'lab') {
      options.getProvider = function () { return window.labWallet || null; };
    }

    var wired = S.walletIdentity.register(options);

    function paint(state) {
      document.querySelector('[data-test="wallet-status"]').textContent =
        state.status + (state.address ? ':' + state.address : '');
      document.querySelector('[data-test="wallet-provider"]').textContent = state.providerName || '';
    }
    wired.source.subscribe(paint);
    paint(wired.source.current());
  })();
</script>
